2:{"type": "memory", "t": 1791232337.324, "agent": "runner", "entries": 6, "text": "# Memory for this patient\n\nWritten by the system, not by the agent: one entry per accepted brief, and one per clinician decision on a proposed action. Newest last.\n\n## 2026-10-05 20:13 UTC\nBrief accepted (run 20261005-160528-edf3ee).\n- next step: Assess for active decompensated heart failure first.\n- next step: Repeat BMP, magnesium, renal function, and BNP urgently.\n- next step: Hold potassium chloride only after doctor approval of medication-safety proposal 103.\n- next step: Rebuild the readmission-prevention plan around adherence and access.\n- next step: Clarify guideline-directed medical therapy gaps once potassium and volume are stabilized.\n- next step: If potassium remains elevated, have the doctor reassess lisinopril and spironolactone.\n- proposed action #99 (lab_request): Urgent electrolyte, magnesium, renal function, and heart-failure-status labs to reassess potassium 5.6 mmol/L, sodium 133 mmol/L, eGFR 42 mL/min/1.73m2, and BNP 1410 pg/mL. [SQL:lab_result]\n- proposed action #100 (patient_message): Message patient to keep the HF visit, bring all medication bottles, track daily weights, report worsening swelling or orthopnea, and seek urgent help for severe symptoms. [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013] [SQL:medication]\n- proposed action #101 (follow_up): Urgent HF-clinic follow-up with transport/cost support and review of home-health alternatives because readmissions are linked to adherence, monitoring, and affordability barriers. [SQL:appointment] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012] [SQL:referral]\n- proposed action #103 (medication_change): Medication-safety proposed holding potassium chloride 20 mEq daily pending urgent repeat BMP and clinician review, and this medication change awaits the doctor under policy CP-02. [SQL:medication] [SQL:lab_result]\n\n## 2026-10-05 20:13 UTC\nClinician approved action #103: Medication change: hold Potassium chloride. Result: medication 5904 (Potassium chloride): hold by physician order.\n\n## 2026-10-05 20:13 UTC\nClinician approved action #101: Follow-up: Heart failure clinic visit within 7 days. Result: appointment 40 requested within 7 days.\n\n## 2026-10-05 20:13 UTC\nClinician rejected action #100: Message: Important update about your heart health.\n\n## 2026-10-05 20:13 UTC\nClinician approved action #99: Lab request: basic metabolic panel, BNP, magnesium. Result: lab_order 18 ordered: [\"basic metabolic panel\",\"BNP\",\"magnesium\"].\n\n## 2026-10-05 20:27 UTC\nBrief accepted (run 20261005-162223-09bd54).\n- next step: Assess active decompensated HF first\n- next step: Review repeat labs before changing the HF regimen\n- next step: Have the doctor decide on holding spironolactone under CP-02\n- next step: Fix the readmission pathway, not just the medication list\n- next step: Reassess HFrEF disease-modifying therapy after stabilization\n- proposed action #110 (lab_request): Request hemoglobin A1c and CBC to update diabetes and general post-discharge status while renal/electrolyte HF labs are already addressed by prior ordering [SQL:condition].\n- proposed action #109 (patient_message): Send an appointment-logistics message focused on completing the upcoming visit plan and access coordination, avoiding the previously rejected symptom/weight/bottle-reminder content, because transport and cost barriers are documented [SQL:referral] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013].\n- proposed action #111 (follow_up): Arrange HF clinic follow-up within 14 days to maintain timely transitional care for a patient with two HF readmissions in 90 days [SQL:patient] [SQL:appointment].\n- proposed action #113 (medication_change): Medication-safety proposes holding spironolactone for potassium 5.6 mmol/L with eGFR 42 mL/min/1.73m2, and this medication change awaits the doctor under policy CP-02 [SQL:lab_result] [SQL:medication].\n", "store": "OracleStore (langgraph-oracledb)", "checkpointer": "OracleSaver (langgraph-oracledb)"}
