14:{"type": "thought", "t": 1791232369.47, "agent": "chart-analyst", "text": "Patient Y (SYN-Y), a 72-year-old female (born 1954) [SQL:patient], is scheduled for a post-discharge heart failure clinic visit in one week [SQL:patient]. She has been readmitted twice in the last 90 days for heart failure [SQL:patient].\n\n**Heart Failure Readmissions:**\n*   **2026-08-30**: Second readmission in 90 days, with weight up 3.4 kg from discharge. Potassium was 5.6 mmol/L on admission while taking spironolactone, lisinopril, and potassium chloride. Potassium chloride was held during this stay. eGFR was 42 mL/min/1.73m2 and Sodium 133 mmol/L [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011].\n*   **2026-07-19**: Readmitted 41 days after discharge with orthopnoea. Patient reported stopping afternoon furosemide to avoid frequent urination. No home scale was available at the time. Discharged 2026-07-24 with a scale provided by social work [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009].\n*   **2026-06-03**: Admitted with dyspnoea and leg oedema. BNP was 980 pg/mL. Echo EF 30%, unchanged. Discharged 2026-06-08 on furosemide 40 mg twice daily with daily-weights instruction sheet [SYN-Y-NOTE-0008].\n\n**Latest Labs:**\n*   **Potassium**: Latest value 5.6 mmol/L on 2026-08-30 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011].\n*   **eGFR**: Latest value 42 mL/min/1.73m2 on 2026-08-30 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011].\n*   **Sodium**: Latest value 133 mmol/L on 2026-08-30 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011].\n*   **BNP**: Latest value 980 pg/mL on 2026-06-03 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0008].\n\n**Active Medications:**\n*   Potassium chloride was on the discharge medication list on 2026-09-04, despite being held during the prior hospital stay [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012]. The patient reports taking the potassium tablet as of 2026-09-15 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013].\n*   Spironolactone and Lisinopril were being taken together with potassium chloride when the patient was readmitted with hyperkalemia on 2026-08-30 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011].\n*   Furosemide refill was picked up 9 days late on 2026-07-30 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010]. Patient reported stopping afternoon furosemide dose prior to 2026-07-19 readmission [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009].\n\n**Appointments/Referrals:**\n*   Heart failure clinic appointment scheduled for 2026-09-18 [SQL:appointment].\n*   Heart failure clinic visit requested for 2026-10-12 [SQL:appointment].\n*   Home health nursing referral declined by patient due to cost on 2026-09-04 [SQL:referral, SYN-Y-NOTE-0012].\n*   Transport assistance referral requested by patient on 2026-09-15 [SQL:referral].\n\n**Care Gaps:**\n*   No SGLT2 inhibitor documented; reason not documented [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012].\n*   Patient reports weight gain of 3.1 kg above discharge weight and new ankle swelling as of 2026-09-15 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013].\n*   Patient reports needing two pillows to sleep as of 2026-09-15 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013].\n*   Patient expressed difficulty with medication copay for eight medicines on a fixed income on 2026-07-30 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010]."}
