96:{"type": "tool", "t": 1791232570.353, "agent": "medication-safety", "name": "propose_medication_change", "args": "{\"citations\": \"[SYN-Y-NOTE-0011] [MEDQUAD-01695#chunk-0] [MEDQUAD-02311#chunk-0] [PMID-14551367]\", \"reason\": \"Patient SYN-Y, a 72F with HFrEF, experienced hyperkalemia (potassium 5.6 mmol/L) and reduced eGFR (42 mL/min/1.73m2) on 2026-08-30 while on spironolactone and lisinopril [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011]. Although potassium chloride was subsequently held, spironolactone is a potassium-sparing diuretic that can exacerbate hyperkalemia, especially with impaired renal function [MEDQUAD-01695#chunk-0, MEDQUAD-02311#chunk-0, PMID-14551367]. Holding spironolactone is a necessary step to mitigate the risk of further hyperkalemia and acute kidney injury.\", \"escalation_id\": 17, \"medication\": \"Spironolactone\", \"change\": \"hold\"}"}
