150:{"type": "tool", "t": 1791233122.714, "agent": "lead", "name": "PreVisitBrief", "args": "{\"snapshot\": \"Jordan Ellis is a woman born in 1954 with HFrEF with EF 30% and a scheduled post-discharge heart failure clinic visit after two readmissions in 90 days. [SQL:patient] [SQL:condition] [SQL:appointment] The readmission pattern is most consistent with recurrent congestion plus practical adherence/access barriers: she stopped afternoon furosemide on bus days, picked up furosemide 9 days late, declined home health because of cost, asked for transport help, and reported medication copay difficulty. [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010#chunk-0] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0] The clinic should address active decompensation and hyperkalemia first because she reported new ankle swelling, two-pillow sleep, and weight 3.1 kg above discharge, while the latest potassium was 5.6 mmol/L with eGFR 42 mL/min/1.73m2 and BNP 1410 pg/mL. [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0] [SQL:lab_result]\", \"what_changed\": [{\"headline\": \"Congestion/readmission risk\", \"detail\": \"Patient Y had HF admissions on 2026-06-03, 2026-07-19, and 2026-08-30, with the July readmission associated with stopping afternoon furosemide on bus days and the August readmission associated with 3.4 kg weight gain from discharge. [SQL:encounter] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011#chunk-0] Since the last brief, the key charted near-term concern remains the 2026-09-15 call reporting new ankle swelling, two-pillow sleep, and weight 73.9 kg, which was 3.1 kg above discharge. [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0]\"}, {\"headline\": \"Potassium and kidney function\", \"detail\": \"Potassium rose from 4.6 mmol/L on 2026-06-03 to 4.9 mmol/L on 2026-07-19 and 5.6 mmol/L on 2026-08-30. [SQL:lab_result] eGFR fell from 51 mL/min/1.73m2 on 2026-06-03 to 46 on 2026-07-19 and 42 on 2026-08-30. [SQL:lab_result] The calculated eGFR slope was -0.00028 mL/min/1.73m2/year, which is less negative and therefore slower decline than the type 2 diabetes cohort p10 -5.88 and p50 -2.75 mL/min/1.73m2/year benchmarks. [SQL:lab_result] [SQL:cohort_benchmark]\"}, {\"headline\": \"BNP and sodium\", \"detail\": \"BNP increased from 980 pg/mL on 2026-06-03 to 1240 pg/mL on 2026-07-19 and 1410 pg/mL on 2026-08-30, paralleling recurrent admissions and ongoing congestion symptoms. [SQL:lab_result] [SQL:encounter] Sodium was 133 mmol/L on 2026-08-30, adding concern for higher-risk decompensated HF physiology. [SQL:lab_result]\"}, {\"headline\": \"Medication-list conflict after potassium hold\", \"detail\": \"Potassium chloride was held during the 2026-08-30 hospitalization because potassium was 5.6 mmol/L while the patient was taking spironolactone and lisinopril. [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011#chunk-0] The discharge medication list later included potassium chloride and the patient reported taking the potassium tablet on 2026-09-15, although memory indicates the clinician subsequently approved and executed a potassium chloride hold. [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0]\"}, {\"headline\": \"Access plan status\", \"detail\": \"HF follow-up within 14 days was requested on 2026-09-04 and the HF clinic appointment is scheduled for 2026-09-18, with another HF clinic visit requested for 2026-10-12. [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0] [SQL:appointment] A home-health nursing referral was declined because of cost and a transport-assistance referral was requested after the patient asked about transportation. [SQL:referral] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0]\"}], \"medications_to_review\": [{\"medication\": \"Furosemide 40 mg twice daily\", \"concern\": \"missed doses and recurrent congestion\", \"chart_evidence\": \"Furosemide is active at 40 mg twice daily. [SQL:medication] The patient stopped afternoon furosemide doses to avoid frequent urination on bus days and later picked up a furosemide refill 9 days late. [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010#chunk-0]\", \"sources\": \"[SQL:medication] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0] [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010#chunk-0]\"}, {\"medication\": \"Lisinopril 10 mg once daily\", \"concern\": \"hyperkalemia risk; medication-safety prop ..."}
