{"type": "delegate", "t": 1791233188.49, "agent": "lead", "subagent": "guideline-researcher", "request": "The prior guideline search returned only CKD potassium references. Please search MEDQUAD again for Patient Y-related clinical reference topics and return 3-6 citable findings with exact MEDQUAD ids and titles. Specific questions: 1) Heart failure symptoms/signs: ankle/leg swelling, dyspnea, orthopnea, cough at night/lying down, rapid weight gain/fluid buildup. 2) Heart failure treatment/follow-up self-care: weighing, salt restriction, when to call clinician, diuretics if available. 3) CKD high potassium risk and diet potassium reduction. 4) Diabetes/CKD metformin or diabetes medicine kidney cautions, if available. 5) Any patient-reference information about ACE inhibitors, aldosterone antagonists, or potassium-sparing drugs increasing potassium or requiring lab monitoring. 6) If no results for medication classes or SGLT2/HFrEF therapy, explicitly say no useful MEDQUAD result. Return only findings that cite MEDQUAD ids actually returned by search."}
{"type": "delegate", "t": 1791233188.49, "agent": "lead", "subagent": "evidence-researcher", "request": "The prior evidence search returned only one useful PMID. Please search PubMed broadly and return 5-8 valid PMID-cited findings for Patient Y's questions. Use only ids returned by your current search. Questions: 1) early post-discharge/post-ED follow-up after HF and outcomes; 2) HF clinic, multidisciplinary disease-management, nurse-led management, or telemonitoring effects on HF hospitalization/readmission/mortality; 3) SGLT2 inhibitor RCTs in HFrEF or HF including patients with/without diabetes and kidney function subgroup if available; 4) hyperkalemia in HF/CKD on ACEi/ARB/MRA/RAASi and potassium binders enabling RAASi continuation; 5) BNP/NT-proBNP prognostic value after HF hospitalization; 6) hyponatremia in HF prognosis; 7) medication adherence/cost/access barriers and HF readmission risk. Return exact PMID ids, article titles, and concise findings. Avoid citing any id unless current search returns it."}
