28:{"type": "thought", "t": 1791232771.498, "agent": "chart-analyst", "text": "Patient Y (Jordan Ellis), female, born 1954, is in a situation of heart failure with two readmissions in 90 days, with a post-discharge heart failure clinic visit scheduled for next week [SQL:patient].\n\n**Heart Failure History and Readmissions:**\n*   Heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (EF 30%) was diagnosed on 2020-03-02 [SQL:condition].\n*   Patient Y had a hospital admission on 2026-06-03 [SQL:encounter].\n*   Patient Y was readmitted on 2026-07-19 with orthopnoea; a likely driver was the patient stopping the afternoon furosemide dose to avoid frequent urination on bus days, and not having a home scale [SQL:encounter], [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0].\n*   Patient Y was readmitted again on 2026-08-30; a likely driver was a 3.4 kg weight gain from discharge [SQL:encounter], [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011#chunk-0].\n\n**Latest Labs and Trends:**\n*   **Potassium:** Latest value 5.6 mmol/L on 2026-08-30 [SQL:lab_result]. Previous values were 4.9 mmol/L on 2026-07-19 and 4.6 mmol/L on 2026-06-03 [SQL:lab_result], indicating an increasing trend.\n*   **Sodium:** Latest value 133.0 mmol/L on 2026-08-30 [SQL:lab_result].\n*   **eGFR:** Latest value 42.0 mL/min/1.73m2 on 2026-08-30 [SQL:lab_result]. Previous values were 46.0 mL/min/1.73m2 on 2026-07-19 and 51.0 mL/min/1.73m2 on 2026-06-03 [SQL:lab_result], indicating a decreasing trend.\n*   **BNP:** Latest value 1410.0 pg/mL on 2026-08-30 [SQL:lab_result]. Previous values were 1240.0 pg/mL on 2026-07-19 and 980.0 pg/mL on 2026-06-03 [SQL:lab_result], indicating an increasing trend.\n*   No HbA1c or CBC results were found in the chart.\n\n**eGFR Slope and Cohort Benchmark:**\n*   Patient Y's eGFR slope is -0.00028 mL/min/1.73m2 per year [SQL:lab_result].\n*   The cohort benchmark for Type 2 diabetes eGFR change per year shows p10 at -5.88, p50 at -2.75, and p90 at 0.99 mL/min/1.73m2 per year [SQL:cohort_benchmark]. Patient Y's eGFR decline is significantly slower (less negative) than the p10 and p50 of the cohort.\n\n**Current Medications and Concerns:**\n*   Active medications include Aspirin 81 mg once daily, Atorvastatin 80 mg once daily, Carvedilol 6.25 mg twice daily, Furosemide 40 mg twice daily, Lisinopril 10 mg once daily, Metformin 500 mg twice daily, and Spironolactone 25 mg once daily [SQL:medication].\n*   **Potassium chloride hold approved/executed:** Potassium chloride was held during the hospital stay on 2026-08-30 due to hyperkalemia (K 5.6 mmol/L) while the patient was also taking spironolactone and lisinopril [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011#chunk-0]. However, potassium chloride was back on the discharge medication list on 2026-09-04 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0], and the patient reported taking the potassium tablet on 2026-09-15 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0].\n*   **Spironolactone hold was proposed before but not documented as clinician decision in memory, so verify status before flagging:** Spironolactone 25 mg once daily is currently active [SQL:medication] and was being taken when potassium was 5.6 mmol/L on 2026-08-30 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0011#chunk-0], indicating it was not held.\n*   **Medication adherence concerns:** Patient stopped afternoon furosemide doses to avoid frequent urination [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0]. Furosemide refill was picked up 9 days late [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010#chunk-0].\n*   **Medication cost concerns:** Patient reported difficulty with copay for eight medications on a fixed income [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010#chunk-0].\n*   **Care gap:** No SGLT2 inhibitor is documented, and the reason is not documented [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0].\n\n**Appointments, Referrals, and Orders Status:**\n*   **HF follow-up requested:** Follow-up in heart failure clinic within 14 days was requested on 2026-09-04 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0].\n*   A Heart failure clinic appointment is scheduled for 2026-09-18 [SQL:appointment].\n*   Another Heart failure clinic visit is requested for 2026-10-12 [SQL:appointment].\n*   **BMP/BNP/magnesium ordered:** No explicit orders for BMP/BNP/magnesium were found in the chart.\n*   A referral for home health nursing was declined on 2026-09-04 due to cost [SQL:referral], [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0].\n*   A referral for transport assistance was requested on 2026-09-15 after the patient inquired about transport [SQL:referral], [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0].\n\n**Symptoms, Adherence, Cost/Transport/Home-Health Barriers from Notes:**\n*   **Symptoms:** Patient was admitted with dyspnoea and leg oedema on 2026-06-03 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0008#chunk-0]. Readmitted with orthopnoea on 2026-07-19 [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0]. On 2026-09-15, patient reported new ankle swelling and needing two pillows to sleep, with a weight of 73.9 kg (3.1 kg above discharge weight) [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0].\n*   **Adherence:** Patient admitted to stopping afternoon furosemide doses to avoid frequent urination [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0]. Furosemide refill was picked up 9 days late [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010#chunk-0]. On 2026-09-15, patient reported taking all medicines, including the potassium tablet [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0].\n*   **Barriers:** Patient declined home health nursing due to cost [SYN-Y-NOTE-0012#chunk-0]. Patient expressed difficulty with medication copays on a fixed income [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010#chunk-0]. Patient inquired about transport assistance [SYN-Y-NOTE-0013#chunk-0].\n\n**Citable Source IDs and Titles/Table Descriptions:**\n*   [SQL:patient]: Patient demographics and visit reason.\n*   [SQL:condition]: Patient's medical conditions.\n*   [SQL:encounter]: Patient's hospital admissions and readmissions.\n*   [SQL:lab_result]: Patient's lab results (Potassium, Sodium, Creatinine, eGFR, BNP).\n*   [SQL:medication]: Patient's active medications.\n*   [SQL:appointment]: Patient's scheduled and requested appointments.\n*   [SQL:referral]: Patient's referrals.\n*   [SQL:cohort_benchmark]: Cohort comparison data for eGFR change.\n*   [SYN-Y-NOTE-0008#chunk-0]: Patient Y - Hospital admission (2026-06-03) note.\n*   [SYN-Y-NOTE-0009#chunk-0]: Patient Y - Hospital readmission (2026-07-19) note.\n*   [SYN-Y-NOTE-0010#chunk-0]: Patient Y - Pharmacy n ..."}
