{"type": "thought", "t": 1791233198.141, "agent": "guideline-researcher", "text": "*   **MEDQUAD-03656#chunk-0**: Lifestyle changes for heart failure treatment include reducing salt and fluid intake, following a heart-healthy diet, and engaging in physical activity. These measures are crucial for managing the condition and preventing its progression [MEDQUAD-03656#chunk-0].\n*   **MEDQUAD-03651#chunk-0**: Preventing heart failure involves maintaining healthy cholesterol and blood pressure, managing diabetes, and limiting salt intake to prevent fluid buildup and high blood pressure. For older adults, a sodium intake of 1500 mg per day is recommended [MEDQUAD-03651#chunk-0].\n*   **MEDQUAD-03657#chunk-0**: Diuretics are among the medications used to manage heart failure, specifically to reduce fluid buildup. Other medications include ACE inhibitors, beta blockers, and digoxin, each working to improve heart function in different ways [MEDQUAD-03657#chunk-0].\n\nThe reference text does not explicitly cover \"when to call clinician\" in the provided snippets. I will continue searching for the remaining questions."}
